Kogut <bulwersator@gmail.com> writes:

> What will break save/bone compatibility?
> I know that it will be caused by adding new monsters/objects. I

The number of monsters and objects, as you suspect, also artifacts are
counted to version.entity_count.
The sizes of structs flag, obj, monst and you are counted to
version.struct_sizes.
The state of compile time options REINCARNATION, SINKS, KOPS, MAIL,
TOURIST, STEED, GOLDOBJ, TEXTCOLOR, INSURANCE, ELBERETH, EXP_ON_BOTL,
SCORE_ON_BOTL, ZEROCOMP and RLECOMP are bitmapped to
version.feature_set.
And VERSION_MAJOR, VERSION_MINOR, PATCHLEVEL and EDITLEVEL are used to
calculate version.incarnation.

Of course, also some other differencies not shown in the version struct
may also cause files to fail loading, or maybe behaving not the expected
way.  
But I suppose most architectural differences also affect those figures.

